            },
            {
              q: "What are the key features of the Left Atrium?",
              a: "• Receives 4 pulmonary veins.<br>• Mostly smooth-walled.<br>• <b>Clinical Note:</b> It is the most posterior chamber. Enlargement (e.g., in mitral stenosis) can compress the <b>esophagus</b>, causing dysphagia."
            },
            {
              q: "What are the key features of the Left Ventricle?",
