            },
            {
              q: "What is an EPSP vs IPSP?",
              a: "EPSP (excitatory postsynaptic potential) — depolarization, Na+ or Ca2+ influx, moves membrane toward threshold | IPSP (inhibitory postsynaptic potential) — hyperpolarization, K+ efflux or Cl- influx, moves membrane away from threshold | Summation of EPSPs/IPSPs determines if AP fires"
            },
            {
              q: "What is temporal vs spatial summation?",
              a: "Temporal summation — rapid repeated stimuli from ONE presynaptic neuron → EPSPs summate over time | Spatial summation — simultaneous stimuli from MULTIPLE presynaptic neurons → EPSPs summate across membrane | Both mechanisms for reaching threshold"
            },
            {
              q: "What is the role of Ca2+ in synaptic transmission?",
