                                      "q": "Mechanism of action of Cetuximab?",
                                      "a": "Monoclonal antibody against EGFR (Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Mechanism of action of Rasburicase?",
                                      "a": "Recombinant uricase that catalyzes the metabolism of uric acid to allantoin."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Common use for Rasburicase in Oncology?",
                                      "a": "Prevention and treatment of Tumor Lysis Syndrome.\n\nClinical \"Best\" Practices (Quick Hitters)"
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Best drug for treating hypertensive emergency in a patient with aortic dissection?",
                                      "a": "Esmolol (requires rapid heart rate and BP control)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Preferred anticoagulant for a pregnant patient with a DVT?",
                                      "a": "Low Molecular Weight <b>Heparin</b> (LMWH), such as Enoxaparin."
                            },
                            {
