                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Definitive cell type seen in <b>Extramammary Paget Disease</b>?",
                                      "a": "Large, malignant epithelial cells with <b>PAS</b>+, Keratin+, and <b>S100</b>- staining."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Key distinction between Vulvar <b>Paget Disease</b> and Melanoma?",
                                      "a": "Paget cells are <b>PAS</b>+ and Keratin+, while Melanoma is <b>S100</b>+."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Most common primary malignancy of the vagina?",
                                      "a": "Squamous cell carcinoma, usually associated with high-risk <b>HPV</b>."
