                                      "q": "Definition of <b>Endometriosis</b>?",
                                      "a": "Ectopic endometrial glands and stroma outside the uterine cavity."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Most common site for <b>Endometriosis</b>?",
                                      "a": "The ovaries (often forming \"<b>Chocolate Cysts</b>\")."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Common clinical triad of <b>Endometriosis</b>?",
                                      "a": "Dysmenorrhea, dyspareunia, and infertility."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Most common benign tumor in females?",
                                      "a": "<b>Leiomyoma</b> (<b>Fibroid</b>)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Characteristic gross appearance of a <b>Leiomyoma</b>?",
                                      "a": "Multiple, well-circumscribed, firm, gray-white whorled masses."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Key distinction between <b>Leiomyoma</b> and <b>Leiomyosarcoma</b>?",
                                      "a": "Leiomyosarcomas are solitary, show necrosis, hemorrhage, and high mitotic activity.\n\nOvarian Pathology"
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Most common type of Ovarian Tumor?",
                                      "a": "Surface epithelial tumors."
                            },
