                                      "a": "Abrasion is a superficial scrape; Laceration is a tear caused by blunt force (shows tissue bridging)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Defining feature of an Incised Wound?",
                                      "a": "A clean-cut wound longer than it is deep, caused by a sharp object (no tissue bridging)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Characteristics of a Contact Gunshot Wound?",
                                      "a": "Muzzle imprint, soot, and seared skin; \"stellate\" appearance over bone."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "What is \"Stippling\" or \"Tattooing\" in forensics?",
                                      "a": "Small abrasions on skin caused by unburnt gunpowder particles in intermediate-range GSWs."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Primary finding in <b>Carbon Monoxide</b> (CO) poisoning?",
                                      "a": "Cherry-red discoloration of skin and organs."
                            },
