                                      "q": "Primary finding in <b>Cyanide</b> poisoning?",
                                      "a": "Bitter almond odor and \"brick-red\" skin."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Characteristics of a 1st-degree burn?",
                                      "a": "Epidermis only; painful, red, no blisters."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Characteristics of a 2nd-degree burn?",
                                      "a": "Epidermis and dermis; painful with blisters."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Definition of \"Rule of Nines\"?",
                                      "a": "Method used to estimate the total body surface area (TBSA) affected by burns."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Typical finding in exit wounds of GSWs?",
                                      "a": "Larger, irregular, and lack soot or stippling."
                            },
                            {
