                                      "a": "Instantaneous onset of <b>rigor mortis</b> in a specific muscle group, usually associated with violent death."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Main forensic finding in Drowning?",
                                      "a": "Frothy fluid in airways and \"washerwoman\" skin (though non-specific)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Finding in \"Dry Drowning\"?",
                                      "a": "Laryngospasm prevents water from entering the lungs."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Difference between \"Manner of Death\" and \"Cause of Death\"?",
                                      "a": "Cause is the injury/disease (e.g., GSW); Manner is the legal category (e.g., Homicide, Suicide, Accident)."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Common finding in Manual Strangulation?",
                                      "a": "Fractured hyoid bone and petechial hemorrhages in the conjunctiva."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Forensic indicator of Antemortem vs. Postmortem bruising?",
                                      "a": "Antemortem bruises show cellular infiltration and inflammatory response."
                            },
                            {
                                      "q": "Definition of <b>Saponification</b> (Adipocere)?",
