            {
                        "q": "What is the most significant risk associated with trying to primary-anastamose an unprepared, acutely obstructed colon?",
                        "a": "High rate of anastomotic leak and subsequent fecal peritonitis."
            },
            {
                        "q": "What surgical procedure involves resecting the diseased bowel, creating a proximal end-colostomy, and sewing closed the distal rectal pouch?",
                        "a": "A Hartmann's Procedure."
            },
            {
                        "q": "Under what circumstances is a Hartmann's Procedure favored over a primary anastomosis in colorectal surgery?",
                        "a": "In the setting of gross purulent/fecal peritonitis, hemodynamic instability, or severe malnutrition where an anastomosis will not heal safely."
            },
