                        "a": "It significantly upgrades the tumor staging and indicates a much higher risk of regional and systemic recurrence."
            },
            {
                        "q": "If a sentinel lymph node biopsy is positive for melanoma micrometastasis, what is the next step according to modern guidelines?",
                        "a": "Therapeutic nodal observation with ultrasound and systemic immunotherapy, rather than an immediate completion lymph node dissection."
            },
            {
                        "q": "What is the classic surgical procedure for a resectable adenocarcinoma located in the head of the pancreas?",
                        "a": "A Pancreaticoduodenectomy, universally known as the Whipple procedure."
            },
            {
                        "q": "What specific structures are entirely removed during a standard classic Whipple procedure?",
                        "a": "The head of the pancreas, duodenum, distal stomach (antrum), gallbladder, and common bile duct."
            },
            {
                        "q": "What is the most common and dangerous life-threatening complication specific to the postoperative course of a Whipple procedure?",
                        "a": "Pancreatic anastomotic leak resulting in a pancreatic fistula, which can digest nearby major vessels and cause catastrophic hemorrhage."
